Z||000000||camon||12-01-2001||10:37 PM||||Sorry about the length of this but I wanted to be as detailed as possible!<P>I'm gonna go back and try to fix my squealing condition and need some advice.<P>I had posted about this before but then got side tracked because of my rear brake rattle and now i'm gonna try to fix this annoying noise again.<P>Here is an overview again:<BR>I have a squeal that is coming from the cars engine compartment. Now I was told that it could be the Alternator (this is quite possible...but want to be 100% sure before tackling this rough job).<BR>The squeal isn't there when you first start the car (when engine is cold). The squeal only starts about 1 minute after running and is gets worse the hotter the engine gets (longer you run). Once the egine is warm the noise stays about the same pitch. It is a very annoying squeal especially when the engine has warmed up. It can be heard in the car with the windows up while at an idle or light throttle. If you rev the engine you can't hear it (not sure in the engine rpm's are drowning it out or if at higher rpm's the squeal goes away). The squeal is coming from the alternater side of the engine but I can't pinpoint it to a direct area of the engine. It isn't a water pump because I had it replaced like 2 months ago and I don't think it is being caused by the belt because it is real tight (only slight movement with heavy finger pressure).<P>Well guy's what do you think....is it the alternator? The guy I bought the car from said it was replaced about 4 months before I bought the car......like 7 monnths total. I notice that if I turn on my manual rad. fan switch I notice a drop in volts (cars amp gauge) and the lights will dim slightly. The car is always at a heavy charge while driving it is right about at the red line and when rad fan switch is on it drops to about 13 and the lights dim. I have no starting problems (it starts fast and strong everytime).<P>So what do you guys think!<P>------------------<BR>   Keith<BR>1987 Fiero GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rumor||12-01-2001||11:29 PM||||A squeal?  Does it sound like "weeeeeeeeee"? Is it constant?  Does the whine change if you press the automatic window buttons, or the gas/brake pedals?  Do you hear it for a second or two if you turn the key (but not start the car)<BR>  Mine does that, and most people here say it's my fuel pump. I will record a sample of it and send out the URL to ya, and you can tell if it is the same sound.  There is a lot of info about changing your fuel pump around, and since I will be doing it next weekend or the following one, I'll let you know what I did and how things turned out.<BR>Cheers!<P>-Rumor<P> 85 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||12-02-2001||02:01 AM||||Might tbe the front bearing in the alternator. I've have had them go out like that before. They will still charge too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-02-2001||09:33 AM||||If it's the alternator bearing, you can find out this way...<BR>Take a long screwdriver or tire tool. Place the pointed end of it against the rear of the alternator housing. Put the other end of it in your ear. Works like a stethescope. If the bearing is shot you'll be able to tell. <BR>If it's not the alternator, poke around with it until you find where the noise is coming from. Be *very careful* of moving pulleys and belts. <BR> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||camon||12-02-2001||12:41 PM||||Rumor:<BR>The sound is constant. It doesn't make it without the car running and it sounds like a VRRRRRRRR (kinda high pitched). It would sound like a car that has power steering trouble and you turn the wheel to hard one way or the other (it makes a sqealing noise).<P>Indiana:<BR>The bearing is what I was told before that it could be. So chances are you may be correct....I just want to be sure of this before tackling this rough alternater drop and install. The only thing that don't make sense is if it is in fact the alternater then why did it go bad so soon (only about 7 months old). Maybe to much tension on the belt????????<P>Raydar:<BR>The screwdriver method won't be nessisary...... I have a mechanics stethiscope (just got to find it). If I can't find the stethiscope I will try the screw driver method!<P>My last option (if I can't asure myself 100% where the noise is coming from) I will try to take it to a garage so a mechanic can here it....maybe they will know right off the bat what the noise is (then i'll fix it myself....don't even want to think what a mechanic would charge for an alternater remove and install job on a fiero).<P>Well thank you guys for the input! <P><P>------------------<BR>   Keith<BR>1987 Fiero GT||||reg||1
